  "details": "As a user that plays PC VR (Quest), I find that when I hit the oculus button after being in a world for quite some time, when I have a few heavy avatars shown, my pc not really being that good despite having 40GB ram, or a mix of the three, that my oculus menu will glitch out, frame drop, and be overall slow with opening and closing it, it would be helpful to open the quick menu and see what time it is using the time of the device running VRChat. It would be helpful for anyone else who might also have this issue, would save them a small walk to their computer if they are standing up, make it so that they don't have to keep getting up from their seat, instances that the user feels immersed or has a fun time that they lose track of it, or if the user cannot get up, due to them having a disability that makes it impossible to do so. Having the option to have the time displayed next to the fps and ping if pinned on top of the quick menu would be helpful for time management.",
